## [Completed] August 17, 2026: Fixed Subpage Navigation Bounds and Overflow
- **Target Files:** [src/index.css](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/index.css), [src/Pricing.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/Pricing.jsx), [src/FAQ.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/FAQ.jsx), [src/Support.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/Support.jsx), [src/Feedback.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/Feedback.jsx), [src/PrivacyPolicy.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/PrivacyPolicy.jsx), [src/TermsOfService.jsx](file:///H:/web3/iota-wallet/website/src/TermsOfService.jsx)
- **Problem:** On subpages, the fixed navbar lacked explicit `left: 0; right: 0; box-sizing: border-box;`, causing the navbar to inherit container padding and push the right-side elements (including the Install button) outside the right edge of the viewport.
- **Remediation:**
  - Pinned `.nav` strictly with `position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;`.
  - Added `.subpage-container` class with proper top clearance (`padding-top: 6.5rem`) across all subpages, removing container padding interference.
  - Added responsive media queries for `.nav`, `.nav-links`, and `.subpage-container` so the Install button and theme/language selectors are always visible and properly padded on all screen sizes.

